<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Prasoon Karmacharya – Machine Learning Scientist</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A minimal, considered portfolio for showcasing applied machine learning, research, and data products."
    />

    <!-- SEO / Open Graph -->
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta
      property="og:title"
      content="Prasoon Karmacharya – Machine Learning Scientist"
    />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Calm, focused applied machine learning work with attention to detail, evaluation, and impact."
    />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://karmaindata.com" />

    <!-- Color scheme hint -->
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />

    <!-- Preload primary font weight to avoid FOUT -->
    <link
      rel="preload"
      href="fonts/poppins-latin-400-normal.woff2"
      as="font"
      type="font/woff2"
      crossorigin
    />
    <link
      rel="preload"
      href="fonts/poppins-latin-600-normal.woff2"
      as="font"
      type="font/woff2"
      crossorigin
    />

    <!-- Styles -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles/main.css" />

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link
      rel="icon"
      href="assets/favicon.svg"
      type="image/svg+xml"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

    {% set home_root = "" %}
    {% include "partials/header.html" %}

    <main id="main" class="site-main">
      <section
        id="top"
        class="hero"
        aria-labelledby="hero-title"
      >
        <h1 id="hero-title">
          Hello, I'm <span class="hero__name">Prasoon</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero__lede">
          I build practical machine learning systems that survive contact with reality.
        </p>

        <dl class="hero-meta">
          <div class="hero-meta__item">
            <dt>Focus</dt>
            <dd>Applied ML, causal inference, A.I. products</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-meta__item">
            <dt>Currently</dt>
            <dd>Open to thoughtful ML &amp; data science roles</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-meta__item">
            <dt>Based in</dt>
            <dd>Greater Boston, MA | Remote-friendly</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section
        id="about"
        class="section section--split"
        aria-labelledby="about-title"
      >
        <div class="section__header">
          <h2 id="about-title">About</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section__body">
          <p>
            I work on the parts of machine learning that have to work when the paper
            ends: turning messy, shifting data and ambiguous goals into well-posed
            problems, robust pipelines, and models that actually get used.
          </p>
          <p>
            My experience spans experimentation, causal inference, and production
            ML systems: defining metrics, designing experiments, building features,
            and partnering with engineers and stakeholders to ship data products
            that move the right numbers, not just the easy ones.
          </p>
          <p>
            I care about clarity: clear problem statements, clear interfaces between
            models and product, and clear communication with non-technical partners.
            This site is intentionally minimal – a small set of projects that show
            how I think, not an exhaustive catalog.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        id="experience"
        class="section section--split section--flipped"
        aria-labelledby="experience-title"
      >
        <div class="section__header">
          <h2 id="experience-title">Experience</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section__body">
          <ol class="timeline">
            <li class="timeline__item">
              <div class="timeline__meta">
                <span class="timeline__role">Senior Machine Learning Scientist</span>
                <span class="timeline__org">Product Company</span>
                <span class="timeline__time">2022 – Present</span>
              </div>
              <p class="timeline__summary">
                Leading applied ML work for user-facing products: defining problem
                statements, designing experiments, and taking models from notebook
                to production in close partnership with engineering.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li class="timeline__item">
              <div class="timeline__meta">
                <span class="timeline__role">Data Scientist</span>
                <span class="timeline__org">Analytics &amp; Growth Team</span>
                <span class="timeline__time">2019 – 2022</span>
              </div>
              <p class="timeline__summary">
                Owning metrics, experimentation, and causal analysis for core
                product surfaces, helping teams choose sensible metrics and avoid
                being misled by noisy data.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li class="timeline__item">
              <div class="timeline__meta">
                <span class="timeline__role">Research Assistant</span>
                <span class="timeline__org">University Lab</span>
                <span class="timeline__time">2015 – 2019</span>
              </div>
              <p class="timeline__summary">
                Working on ML and statistics-heavy projects with faculty and peers,
                focusing on reproducible analysis, careful evaluation, and clear
                write-ups.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        id="projects"
        class="section section--split"
        aria-labelledby="projects-title"
      >
        <div class="section__header">
          <h2 id="projects-title">Selected projects</h2>
          <p class="section__kicker">
            A few applied ML projects from the last few years. Happy to share
            deeper write-ups, notebooks, or code samples on request.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="section__body">
        <div class="project-accordion">
          <details class="project-accordion__item">
            <summary class="project-accordion__header">
              <div class="project-accordion__lead">
                <h3 class="project-accordion__title">Signal Ledger</h3>
                <p class="project-accordion__brief">
                  End-to-end demand forecasting replacing spreadsheet heuristics
                  with probabilistic forecasts and uncertainty-aware planning.
                </p>
              </div>
              <span class="project-accordion__pill">Forecasting · Product impact</span>
              <span class="project-accordion__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="project-accordion__body">
              <dl class="project-accordion__meta">
                <div>
                  <dt>Role</dt>
                  <dd>Machine learning scientist, tech lead</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Year</dt>
                  <dd>2025</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Highlights</dt>
                  <dd>Feature engineering, time-series modeling, stakeholder calibration</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <a class="project-accordion__link" href="#">
                Request forecasting case study
              </a>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="project-accordion__item">
            <summary class="project-accordion__header">
              <div class="project-accordion__lead">
                <h3 class="project-accordion__title">Experiment Atlas</h3>
                <p class="project-accordion__brief">
                  Unified experimentation framework standardizing metrics, power
                  analysis, and guardrail checks across growth and product teams.
                </p>
              </div>
              <span class="project-accordion__pill">Experimentation · Uplift</span>
              <span class="project-accordion__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="project-accordion__body">
              <dl class="project-accordion__meta">
                <div>
                  <dt>Role</dt>
                  <dd>Data scientist, experimentation lead</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Year</dt>
                  <dd>2023</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Highlights</dt>
                  <dd>A/A tests, CUPED, standardized experiment review process</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <a class="project-accordion__link" href="#">
                View experimentation notes
              </a>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details class="project-accordion__item">
            <summary class="project-accordion__header">
              <div class="project-accordion__lead">
                <h3 class="project-accordion__title">Reader Studio</h3>
                <p class="project-accordion__brief">
                  Content embeddings and lightweight re-ranking powering a reading
                  environment optimized for sustained engagement over raw click-through.
                </p>
              </div>
              <span class="project-accordion__pill">NLP · Personalization</span>
              <span class="project-accordion__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="project-accordion__body">
              <dl class="project-accordion__meta">
                <div>
                  <dt>Role</dt>
                  <dd>Machine Learning scientist, product partner</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Year</dt>
                  <dd>2022</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Highlights</dt>
                  <dd>Embeddings, offline evaluation, human-in-the-loop feedback</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <a class="project-accordion__link" href="#">
                Explore NLP concept notes
              </a>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        id="blog"
        class="section section--split section--flipped"
        aria-labelledby="blog-title"
      >
        <div class="section__header">
          <h2 id="blog-title">Notes &amp; writing</h2>
          <p class="section__kicker">
            Occasional notes on applied machine learning, evaluation, and making
            models behave in the real world.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="section__body">
        <div class="project-accordion">
          {% for post in blogs %}
          <details class="project-accordion__item">
            <summary class="project-accordion__header">
              <div class="project-accordion__lead">
                <h3 class="project-accordion__title">{{ post.title }}</h3>
                <p class="project-accordion__brief">
                  {{ post.description }}
                </p>
              </div>
              <span class="project-accordion__pill">{{ post.pill }}</span>
              <span class="project-accordion__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="project-accordion__body">
              <dl class="project-accordion__meta">
                <div>
                  <dt>Published</dt>
                  <dd>{{ post.published }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Length</dt>
                  <dd>{{ post.read_time }}</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <dt>Topics</dt>
                  <dd>{{ post.topics }}</dd>
                </div>
              </dl>
              <a class="project-accordion__link" href="blog/{{ post.slug }}.html">
                Read article
              </a>
            </div>
          </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        id="contact"
        class="section section--split"
        aria-labelledby="contact-title"
      >
        <div class="section__header">
          <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="section__body">
          <p>
            For roles, collaborations, or interesting ML problems, email is best.
            A short note about the problem space, your data, and how success is
            measured is especially helpful.
          </p>
          <p class="contact__email">
            <a href="mailto:pk425@cornell.edu">pk425@cornell.edu</a>
          </p>
          <p class="contact__secondary">
            Elsewhere, if you prefer. I'm always happy to talk about evaluation,
            experiment design, or making ML systems a little more honest.
          </p>
          <ul class="contact__socials">
            <li>
              <a
                class="contact__social-link"
                href="https://github.com/karma271"
                rel="me noopener"
              >
                <svg
                  class="contact__social-icon"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  focusable="false"
                >
                  <path
                    d="M12 .297c-6.63 0-12 5.373-12 12 0 5.303 3.438 9.8 8.205 11.385.6.113.82-.258.82-.577 0-.285-.01-1.04-.015-2.04-3.338.724-4.042-1.61-4.042-1.61C4.422 18.07 3.633 17.7 3.633 17.7c-1.087-.744.084-.729.084-.729 1.205.084 1.838 1.236 1.838 1.236 1.07 1.835 2.809 1.305 3.495.998.108-.776.417-1.305.76-1.605-2.665-.3-5.466-1.332-5.466-5.93 0-1.31.465-2.38 1.235-3.22-.135-.303-.54-1.523.105-3.176 0 0 1.005-.322 3.3 1.23.96-.267 1.98-.399 3-.405 1.02.006 2.04.138 3 .405 2.28-1.552 3.285-1.23 3.285-1.23.645 1.653.24 2.873.12 3.176.765.84 1.23 1.91 1.23 3.22 0 4.61-2.805 5.625-5.475 5.92.42.36.81 1.096.81 2.22 0 1.606-.015 2.896-.015 3.286 0 .315.21.69.825.57C20.565 22.092 24 17.592 24 12.297c0-6.627-5.373-12-12-12"
                    fill="currentColor"
                  ></path>
                </svg>
                GitHub
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                class="contact__social-link"
                href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/karmacharya"
                rel="me noopener"
              >
                <svg
                  class="contact__social-icon"
                  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                  aria-hidden="true"
                  focusable="false"
                >
                  <path
                    d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433a2.062 2.062 0 1 1 0-4.125 2.062 2.062 0 0 1 0 4.125zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.225 0z"
                    fill="currentColor"
                  ></path>
                </svg>
                LinkedIn
              </a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    {% include "partials/footer_main.html" %}
  </body>
</html>
